//? Title: Wildcard Matching: Whole Fields, Byte Semantics and Suffix Rescans
//? Subtitle: Titanic name filters, an actual last-star trace and a quadratic worst-case family
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A restricted glob has two metacharacters: a star accepts any byte sequence
and a question mark accepts exactly one byte. We apply this language to
`Name` fields in `dm::datasets::titanic()`, separating whole-field filtering
from substring occurrence counting. A trace of the canonical matcher shows
how the most recent star expands; a separate prefix dynamic program explains
the accepted language. The same loop's counters expose a quadratic family,
correcting the tempting inference that monotone star expansion implies
linear total work. A regression involving a star inside the text illustrates
why pattern metacharacters must retain their meaning before literal comparison.
)

\toc

> The data: independent passenger-name fields

The built-in Titanic frame contains 891 passenger records. We treat each
non-null `Name` cell as an independent byte string; matching never bridges
two records. Names include surnames, titles, given names and punctuation.
The query language does not parse those components. The first table and
length distribution describe the strings being filtered.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/wildcard_names.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const auto passengers = dm::datasets::titanic();
  std::print("{}\n",passengers.select({"PassengerId","Name","Survived"}).head(6).to_md());
  const auto lengths = passengers | dm::mutate("name_bytes",[](const auto& row) {
    return static_cast<double>(row.get_string("Name").size());
  });
  std::print("\n{}\n",(lengths | dm::summarise(dm::agg::n("records"),dm::agg::mean("name_bytes","mean_bytes"),
      dm::agg::min("name_bytes","min_bytes"),dm::agg::max("name_bytes","max_bytes"))).to_md(4));
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RPlot::hist(lengths.get_column("name_bytes").values(),25,"name lengths")
      .title("Titanic passenger name fields: byte lengths")
      .x_label("bytes in one Name field").y_label("passengers")
      .size(1000,480).save_svg("build/wildcard_names.svg");
}
```
